{
	"version": 5,
	"id": "Bj_AB-HIS-lvqYVQS",
	"notes": "An Interrogator: an Inquisitor's chosen second, one step from being invested with a rosette of their own — Eisenhorn's and Ravenor's own Interrogators (before their eventual promotions) are the model. Built as a more capable, more independent Inquisitorial Acolyte (Imperium/ Templates/Inquisitorial Acolyte.gct) rather than a separate archetype. Point math: ST 10 (+0), DX 13 (+60), IQ 14 (+80), HT 11 (+10) = 150, plus Will +1 (+5) = 155; advantages +30; disadvantages -37; skills +178. Total 326 points, near the top of framework.md's \"Elite human (200-350)\" tier — appropriate for someone who is, functionally, nearly an Inquisitor already. No psychic abilities here; add from the separate psyker power library if the Interrogator is also a sanctioned psyker.\n",
	"traits": [
		{
			"id": "tHVwYj-T2UJhueGZT",
			"name": "ST",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Chosen for judgment and capability, not physical extremes.\n\nDesign: ST 10 (baseline), 10 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 0
		},
		{
			"id": "tmRptE6jBMRlW9IWs",
			"name": "DX",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A veteran field agent's honed reflexes, a clear step above a rank-and-file acolyte's.\n\nDesign: DX 13 (+3), 20 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 60
		},
		{
			"id": "tOTZ4SLq0Z36gU-qw",
			"name": "IQ",
			"local_notes": "Lore: An Interrogator is entrusted with independent judgment calls an ordinary acolyte never makes.\n\nDesign: IQ 14 (+4), 20 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 80
		},
		{
			"id": "tUdcdFARDpbqfM1Cx",
			"name": "HT",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Years of fieldwork take their toll but also build endurance.\n\nDesign: HT 11 (+1), 10 pts/level (B14).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 10
		},
		{
			"id": "t8X3UYkrYOa8Kg9pD",
			"name": "Will",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Years spent staring down heretics and worse without flinching.\n\nDesign: Will 15 (+1 above the IQ-derived default of 14), 5 pts/level (B16).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 5
		},
		{
			"id": "tjhRqfxzukJVgOVkz",
			"name": "Fit",
			"reference": "B55",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Kept sharp by a dangerous job and, often, an Inquisitor's exacting standards.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Fit (B55), 5 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": 5
		},
		{
			"id": "t2Is9o62GXxFQffZz",
			"name": "Combat Reflexes",
			"reference": "B43",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A veteran of more firefights than an ordinary acolyte survives to see.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Combat Reflexes (B43), 15 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": 15
		},
		{
			"id": "tG0TIQVSrCfG1baA1",
			"name": "Legal Enforcement Powers (Interrogator's Seal)",
			"reference": "B65",
			"local_notes": "Lore: An Interrogator carries a lesser seal of office that grants real, if narrower, authority than a full Inquisitorial rosette — enough to compel Imperial officials' cooperation in their Inquisitor's name, though not to act wholly independently of them.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Legal Enforcement Powers (B65), 2 levels, 10 points — below the Inquisitorial Rosette's 4-level maximum (Imperium/Traits/Imperial Traits.adq).",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Social",
				"Imperium",
				"Inquisition"
			],
			"base_points": 10
		},
		{
			"id": "tH1_4ijiTfgirDvPa",
			"name": "Duty (Inquisition)",
			"reference": "B133",
			"local_notes": "Lore: An acolyte or Interrogator serves at an Inquisitor's word, and an Inquisitor answers to their Ordo and (nominally) the wider Inquisition; refusal is itself grounds for suspicion of heresy.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Duty (B133), hazardous and frequent, as above.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Social",
				"Imperium",
				"Inquisition"
			],
			"base_points": -15
		},
		{
			"id": "tyGA-CTvqDtQL4_YU",
			"name": "Intolerance (Heretics)",
			"reference": "B140",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Years of hunting heresy sharpen this into something close to reflex.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Intolerance (B140), narrow-category cost (-5).",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -5
		},
		{
			"id": "t-mer2N8gcxBC_tb3",
			"name": "Secret (Works for the Inquisition)",
			"reference": "B152",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Inquisitorial agents routinely operate under cover identities; being identified as Inquisition staff can get an agent killed by exactly the people they are investigating, or by a hostile Imperial official who resents being investigated at all.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Secret (B152), moderate exposure risk, -10.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Social",
				"Imperium",
				"Inquisition"
			],
			"base_points": -10
		},
		{
			"id": "tdo2ziOtDesKE-OTT",
			"name": "Overconfidence",
			"reference": "B148",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A rising star's confidence in their own judgment, not always warranted.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Overconfidence (B148), -5.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -5
		},
		{
			"id": "t0xnI-bQyMw-LmQTn",
			"name": "Measures Everyone Against Their Inquisitor's Standards",
			"local_notes": "Lore: An Interrogator's judgment of competence, loyalty, and piety is shaped by whoever mentored them.\n\nDesign: Quirk (B9), roleplaying flag only.",
			"tags": [
				"Quirk",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -1
		},
		{
			"id": "tquaztHKbreitkgEy",
			"name": "Impatient With Lesser Authority",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Used to invoking an Inquisitor's name and having doors open; less patient with people who can't or won't open them.\n\nDesign: Quirk (B9), roleplaying flag only.",
			"tags": [
				"Quirk",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -1
		}
	],
